==Turkish==
From {{inh|tr|ota|اوينامق|tr=oynamak||to play, perform, risk, disport, move, vibrate, dance, amuse one's self, jest}}, derived from {{etyl|trk-pro|tr}} {{m|trk-pro|*ojun||play}}. See {{etyl|tr|-}} {{m|tr|oyun||play, game}}

Cognate with {{etyl|otk|-}} {{m|otk||tr=oyna-||to play}}, {{etyl|az|-}} {{m|az|oynamaq||to play}}, {{etyl|ba|-}} {{m|ba|уйнау||to play}}, {{etyl|kk|-}} {{m|kk|ойнау||to play}}, {{etyl|kjh|-}} {{m|kjh|ойнирға||to play}}, {{etyl|ky|-}} {{m|ky|ойноо||to play}}, {{etyl|tk|-}} {{m|tk|oýnamak||to play}}, {{etyl|ug|-}} {{m|ug|ئوينىماق||to play}}, {{etyl|uz|-}} {{m|uz|oʻynamoq||to play}}, {{etyl|sah|-}} {{m|sah|оонньоо||to play}}.

===Verb===
{{tr-verb|oynar}}

# to [[play]], [[amuse]] oneself, [[fool]] around
# (for a film or play) to be on, be [[playing]]
# to [[dance]]; to [[gambol]], [[cavort]], [[frisk]] about
# to [[move]], [[stir]], [[budge]], [[hop]]
# to [[fluctuate]], [[move]] back and forth, [[flicker]]
# {{label|tr|transitive}} to [[perform]] (a play), [[play]] (a card)
# to [[risk]], play around with, [[trifle]] with
# to [[monkey]] with, [[tinker]] with, [[tamper]] with

